.Dd August 17, 2026
.Dt RUNTIME_CLI 1
.Os Darwin
.Sh NAME
.Nm runtime_cli
.Nd print headers as RuntimeBrowser sees them, sweep the loaded runtime
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -load Ar image ...
.Op Ar ClassName
.Nm
.Op Fl -load Ar image ...
.Fl -swift Ar TypeName
.Nm
.Fl -sweep Ar directory
.Op Fl -frameworks Ar N
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the command line front end of the RuntimeBrowser model.
.Pp
Without options it prints the Objective-C header of
.Ar ClassName
(NSString by default), with the Swift members and conformances of the class when the image is a Swift one.
.Pp
.Fl -load
loads an image (a framework binary or a dylib) with dlopen(3) first, it may be repeated.
.Pp
.Fl -swift
prints the declaration of a Swift struct, enum or protocol of the loaded images, by qualified name, eg. Foundation.Date or (extension in Foundation):Swift.String.Encoding.
.Pp
.Fl -sweep
loads up to
.Ar N
frameworks (400 by default) of /System/Library/Frameworks and /System/Library/PrivateFrameworks and writes the headers of all the loaded classes and protocols in
.Pa classes/
and
.Pa protocols/ ,
and the declarations of all the Swift types, one file per image, in
.Pa swift/ .
It prints counts and timings on stderr. This is the regression test of the model: sweep before and after a change, then diff -r the two directories.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl runtime_cli NSObject
.Dl runtime_cli --load /System/Library/Frameworks/AppKit.framework/AppKit NSView
.Dl runtime_cli --swift Foundation.Date
.Dl runtime_cli --sweep /tmp/before && ... && runtime_cli --sweep /tmp/after && diff -r /tmp/before /tmp/after
.Sh SEE ALSO
RuntimeBrowser, https://github.com/nst/RuntimeBrowser
